{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"393c131f-4f98-4ba2-9a30-6ba30308ba9c","step":{"id":"s1","script":"Torque measures a force’s turning effect. Here, a twenty-newton force pushes perpendicular to a handle fixed at the pivot.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"title","region":"A1","content":"Torque: turning effect"},{"op":"figure","id":"handle","region":"right","frame":{"x":[-0.8,3.8],"y":[-1,2.8],"axes":"none"},"marks":[{"kind":"point","id":"pivot","at":[0,0],"label":"pivot"},{"kind":"point","id":"tip","at":[3,0]},{"kind":"segment","id":"bar","from":{"at":"pivot"},"to":{"at":"tip"}},{"kind":"segment","id":"force","from":{"at":"tip"},"to":[3,2.2],"arrow":true,"label":"20 N"},{"kind":"segment","id":"action","from":[3,-0.8],"to":[3,2.5],"stroke":"dashed"}]}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"393c131f-4f98-4ba2-9a30-6ba30308ba9c","step":{"id":"s2","script":"The lever arm is the perpendicular distance from the pivot to the force’s line of action. Here, it is thirty centimeters.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"distance","on":"handle","marks":[{"kind":"measure","from":[0,-0.55],"to":[3,-0.55],"label":"0.30 m"},{"kind":"angle","at":{"at":"tip"},"from":[3,1],"to":{"at":"pivot"},"label":"90°"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"rule","anchor":{"el":"title","side":"below","gap":0.12},"latex":"\\tau = Fd_{\\perp}"},{"op":"text","id":"definition","anchor":{"el":"rule","side":"below","gap":0.08},"content":"Use perpendicular distance."}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"393c131f-4f98-4ba2-9a30-6ba30308ba9c","step":{"id":"s3","script":"Multiply force by lever arm: six newton-meters of counterclockwise torque. With the same force, doubling the lever arm doubles the torque.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"turning","on":"handle","marks":[{"kind":"arc","center":{"at":"pivot"},"r":0.65,"start":15,"end":135,"arrow":true},{"kind":"text","at":[1.25,1.3],"text":"6 N·m","size":"normal"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"result","anchor":{"el":"definition","side":"below","gap":0.12},"latex":"\\tau=(20\\,\\mathrm{N})(0.30\\,\\mathrm{m})=6\\,\\mathrm{N\\,m}"}],"checkpoint":{"question":"With the same perpendicular force, what happens to torque if the lever arm doubles?","expected_gist":"Torque doubles."}}}
